   1: # AgentLoop
   2: 
   3: AgentLoop is a local, file-backed orchestration layer for coding agents. It helps a user turn a coding task into a controlled loop:
   4: 
   5: 1. analyze the task
   6: 2. generate task-specific acceptance criteria
   7: 3. wait for human approval
   8: 4. design, implement, test, and review
   9: 5. iterate automatically until the gate passes or the iteration limit is reached
  10: 
  11: It is agent-agnostic. You can use Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot CLI, or a manual runtime if the command can read prompts and write files in the workspace.
  12: 
  13: **Runtime == Coding agent run**
  14: 
  15: ## Capability Map
  16: 
  17: ![AutoPilot AgentLoop capability map](docs/assets/autopilot-capability-map.png)
  18: 
  19: AgentLoop keeps orchestration local: task state, runtime config, generated artifacts, review decisions, and iteration history all stay in `.agentloop/`.
  20: 
  21: ## Quick Start
  22: 
  23: Run these commands from the repository root.
  24: 
  25: ```powershell
  26: python -m agentloop init --detect-runtimes
  27: python -m agentloop runtime list
  28: ```
  29: 
  30: Pick one detected runtime and assign it to every role. For example, with Claude Code:
  31: 
  32: ```powershell
  33: python -m agentloop runtime assign-all claude-code
  34: python -m agentloop runtime verify claude-code --timeout-seconds 120
  35: ```
  36: 
  37: Or with Codex:
  38: 
  39: ```powershell
  40: python -m agentloop runtime assign-all codex
  41: python -m agentloop runtime verify codex --timeout-seconds 120
  42: ```
  43: 
  44: If detection misses a runtime, add a built-in preset first:
  45: 
  46: ```powershell
  47: python -m agentloop runtime add-preset claude-code --replace
  48: python -m agentloop runtime add-preset codex --replace
  49: python -m agentloop runtime add-preset manual --replace
  50: python -m agentloop runtime list
  51: ```
  52: 
  53: ## Run Your First Task
  54: 
  55: Start with a small task that can be verified by tests.
  56: 
  57: ```powershell
  58: python -m agentloop start "实现 doctor 命令，检查 workspace 状态并输出 PASS/FAIL"
  59: ```
  60: 
  61: `start` creates a task and asks the analyst runtime to produce task-specific analysis and acceptance criteria. It stops before implementation so the user can review the goal.
  62: 
  63: List tasks:
  64: 
  65: ```powershell
  66: python -m agentloop tasks
  67: ```
  68: 
  69: Open the generated task artifacts:
  70: 
  71: ```powershell
  72: Get-Content .agentloop\tasks\<task_id>\artifacts\analysis.md
  73: Get-Content .agentloop\tasks\<task_id>\artifacts\acceptance.md
  74: ```
  75: 
  76: Approve only after the analysis and acceptance criteria match what you want:
  77: 
  78: ```powershell
  79: python -m agentloop approve --task-id <task_id>
  80: ```
  81: 
  82: Then run the execution loop:
  83: 
  84: ```powershell
  85: python -m agentloop run --task-id <task_id>
  86: ```
  87: 
  88: AgentLoop will run the configured roles, execute the quality gate, and iterate when review says changes are required.
  89: 
  90: ## Daily Commands
  91: 
  92: ```powershell
  93: python -m agentloop status
  94: python -m agentloop tasks
  95: python -m agentloop status --task-id <task_id>
  96: python -m agentloop cancel --task-id <task_id>
  97: python -m agentloop tasks delete <task_id>
  98: python -m agentloop tasks delete-all
  99: ```
 100: 
 101: Runtime commands:
 102: 
 103: ```powershell
 104: python -m agentloop runtime detect
 105: python -m agentloop runtime list
 106: python -m agentloop runtime assign analyst claude-code
 107: python -m agentloop runtime assign implementer codex
 108: python -m agentloop runtime assign-all claude-code
 109: python -m agentloop runtime verify claude-code --timeout-seconds 120
 110: ```
 111: 
 112: Per-task config commands:
 113: 
 114: ```powershell
 115: python -m agentloop tasks config show --task-id <task_id>
 116: python -m agentloop tasks config set --task-id <task_id> max_iterations 5
 117: python -m agentloop tasks config set --task-id <task_id> --json test_commands '["python -m unittest discover -s tests"]'
 118: python -m agentloop tasks config clear --task-id <task_id>
 119: ```
 120: 
 121: ## Where Files Live
 122: 
 123: ```text
 124: .agentloop/
 125:   config.json                 global runtime and workflow config
 126:   tasks/
 127:     <task_id>/
 128:       state.json              task lifecycle state
 129:       config.json             optional per-task overrides
 130:       artifacts/              analysis, acceptance, design, tests, review output
 131: ```
 132: 
 133: Important generated artifacts usually include:
 134: 
 135: ```text
 136: analysis.md
 137: acceptance.md
 138: acceptance.json
 139: design.md
 140: test_plan.md
 141: review.md
 142: quality_gate.json
 143: ```
 144: 
 145: ## Recommended New-User Flow
 146: 
 147: 1. Run `python -m agentloop init --detect-runtimes`.
 148: 2. Run `python -m agentloop runtime list` and confirm at least one real runtime is available.
 149: 3. Run `python -m agentloop runtime assign-all <runtime>`.
 150: 4. Run `python -m agentloop runtime verify <runtime> --timeout-seconds 120`.
 151: 5. Start a small task with clear testable output.
 152: 6. Review `analysis.md` and `acceptance.md` before approving.
 153: 7. Run the task and inspect generated artifacts after completion.
 154: 
 155: ## Troubleshooting
 156: 
 157: If all roles still show `manual`, runtime detection found commands but no role has been assigned yet. Run:
 158: 
 159: ```powershell
 160: python -m agentloop runtime assign-all claude-code
 161: ```
 162: 
 163: If a Chinese task fails with encoding errors on Windows, make sure you are running the current code. AgentLoop uses UTF-8 subprocess I/O for runtime prompts.
 164: 
 165: If a task is stuck waiting for approval, either approve or cancel it:
 166: 
 167: ```powershell
 168: python -m agentloop approve --task-id <task_id>
 169: python -m agentloop cancel --task-id <task_id>
 170: ```
 171: 
 172: If you want to restart from zero:
 173: 
 174: ```powershell
 175: python -m agentloop tasks delete-all
 176: ```
 177: 
 178: ## Full Documentation
 179: 
 180: See [docs/agentloop-user-guide.md](docs/agentloop-user-guide.md) for the complete user guide, including runtime presets, per-task overrides, task locks, batch operations, and the detailed lifecycle.

